# 16x2 image = four 4-pixel SIMD groups. Row 0 pixel 2b has U=b, V=255-b (b = block number 0..7); every other
# chroma byte is 0 / 255 as shown. Sums of 4 samples are b, so U = floor(b/4) = 0,0,0,0,1,1,1,1 and
# V = floor((255-b + 255 + 0 + 0)/4) = floor((510-b)/4) = 127,127,126,126,126,126,126,125.
# The same image with the input at a 16-byte offset inside its buffer (aligned loads still fine) gives the same bytes.
compress i420 0 2 64 16 8 8 2 1 1 0040ff000041ff000142fe000043ff000244fd000045ff000346fc000047ff000448fb000049ff00054afa00004bff00064cf900004dff00074ef800004fff0000800000008100000082000000830000008400000085000000860000008700000088000000890000008a0000008b0000008c0000008d0000008e0000008f0000
compress nv12 0 2 64 16 16 0 2 1 0 0040ff000041ff000142fe000043ff000244fd000045ff000346fc000047ff000448fb000049ff00054afa00004bff00064cf900004dff00074ef800004fff0000800000008100000082000000830000008400000085000000860000008700000088000000890000008a0000008b0000008c0000008d0000008e0000008f0000
